  "term": "aversive conditioning",
  "definition": "In learning research with laboratory rodents, aversive conditioning is a paradigm in which a previously neutral stimulus or place becomes associated with an aversive experience. The packet states that odours can be paired with aversive states such as fear or malaise, and that animals usually learn this association quickly.",
